{
  "id": "navigation/constructor_calls/02_temporaries",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "constructor_calls",
  "title": "Temporaries",
  "summary": "The class name of a temporary leads to the constructor it calls",
  "prose": "`Widget(1)`, `Widget(2, 3)`, `Widget{4}` and `Widget()` call a constructor\nby the class's name: go-to-definition, declaration, hover, highlights and\nreferences there answer that constructor, and go-to-type-definition the\nclass, a qualified name and a template's specialization alike.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "namespace shapes {\nstruct Circle {\n    Circle(int radius);\n};\n}  // namespace shapes\n\nstruct Widget {\n    Widget();\n    Widget(int size);\n    Widget(int width, int height);\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Box {\n    Box(T value);\n};\n\nvoid build() {\n    auto a = Widget(1);\n    auto b = Widget(2, 3);\n    auto c = Widget{4};\n    auto d = Widget();\n    auto e = shapes::Circle(5);\n    auto f = Box<int>(6);\n}\n",
